{"title":"2022 USAJMO Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Find all pairs of primes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/b/b6b7a40ab0d8178e83fe1b91c511d04b1246059b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(p,q)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/f/a1f8131b9cef2c23369011c1cbc425f2861c026e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p-q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"42\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/5/9d5681a55a654874058d03ade8b5b02eb70ff10d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$pq-q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"16\" /> are both perfect squares.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We first consider the case where one of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/7/f779d95c15f7e41de74cb767f52fe4e7b92c745e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p,q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"28\" height=\"13\" /> is even. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/b/25b803838ba4ded99f094071740c256527784b2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/4/db486c375f5f2f91e5d8cfc22bb5f81e7b17b6fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p-q=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"75\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/9/e79aae3e6668eb5e7d26393ab105447ec6bbc1a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$pq-q=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"84\" height=\"17\" /> which doesn't satisfy the problem restraints. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/4/2249017892bda0490d89aa6d997b953b070b1ba1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"41\" height=\"15\" />, we can set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/5/1f57e4af177fc823565ef3691653176189276098.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p-2=x^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"84\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/9/649bdb20bf9c8fda51249ddaa6a000905f4952ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2p-2=y^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"93\" height=\"20\" /> giving us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/8/e98adbbe1e23540600215e6bbdf21fc5f8c35503.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p=y^2-x^2=(y+x)(y-x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"229\" height=\"21\" />. This forces <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/e/ccebb279d54ee2ff5f2566e3abc5d84516b6356f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y-x=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"17\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/c/08c8a7511667e369a114454e2fbcf886d41314a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p=2x+1\\rightarrow 2x+1=x^2+2 \\rightarrow x=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"310\" height=\"20\" /> giving us the solution <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/5/1a56c7a0994aaddae8d93f28a294cdd16647b61c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(p,q)=(3,2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"103\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nNow assume that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/7/f779d95c15f7e41de74cb767f52fe4e7b92c745e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p,q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"28\" height=\"13\" /> are both odd primes. Set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/d/6bd586d530ea67572359a32943e4b08a1be82ceb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p-q=x^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"84\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/b/9cb5d69761f5deeefed09b8b2df0f5897eb71a34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$pq-q=y^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"92\" height=\"20\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/5/d9571edeb0404c2f17064a601172f22cd2a3546b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(pq-q)-(p-q)=y^2-x^2 \\rightarrow p(q-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"314\" height=\"21\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/8/f48c56a37b8d11aed26b6dba6fb281b68b95d7a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=(y+x)(y-x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"134\" height=\"20\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/e/44e3e7ac887593f91293a07ba670c830f2b88563.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y+x&gt;y-x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"110\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/e/80efb7c86493d1610b4ffd0d4db84f25297b3d31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p | (x+y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"72\" height=\"20\" />. Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/a/55af207869f43d97328748a5cb85274095a6a935.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"39\" height=\"15\" /> is an even integer and since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/4/664b6746f67e0733c4e070dacafae867f279a6ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y+x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/2/1528b38e29e999e114af339c40ba2596e89c8182.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y-x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"11\" /> have the same parity, they both must be even. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c53f9d0d4c5b07bdd60522e24158cfb4cdce43a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y=pk$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"87\" height=\"18\" /> for some positive even integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />. On the other hand, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/0/890b4b10eef2a0ddd9aa9b2fc5948f4c6f198978.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p&gt;p-q=x^2 \\rightarrow p&gt;x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"190\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/c/22c3eeea8247df873151d994d00d2d33928099dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^2-p&gt;pq-q=y^2 \\rightarrow p&gt;y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"235\" height=\"20\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/d/6ada009c28d02a8f1243580682a34d599e23175d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2p&gt;x+y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"86\" height=\"17\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/e/4ce113ee31fb78ac35d184422fb71a915e6da6ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y=p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"16\" />, giving us a contradiction.\n</p><p><br />\nTherefore, the only solution to this problem is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/5/1a56c7a0994aaddae8d93f28a294cdd16647b61c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(p,q)=(3,2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"103\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n~BennettHuang\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_USAJMO\" title=\"2022 USAJMO\">2022 USAJMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_USAJMO_Problems\" title=\"2022 USAJMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=176&amp;year=2022\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2022 USAJMO Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2022 USAJMO Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2022 USAJMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2022 USAJMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_3\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2022 USAJMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2022 USAJMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2022 USAJMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAJMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAJMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAJMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017054047\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.039 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.068 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 198/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1326/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 48/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5601/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   19.821      1 -total\n 68.43%   13.564      1 Template:USAJMO_newbox\n 29.72%    5.891      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:22659:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017054047 and revision id 199238. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}